course: dictionary
lesson: 10276
title: The Torah
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Torah is very important in the Jewish faith. It is the first five books of the Hebrew Bible: Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers and Deuteronomy. «The Torah is the first five books of the Hebrew Bible, handwritten on scrolls that are read in the synagogue with great respect.»
explain: The word Torah can mean three things, so use the words around it to decide which one fits. «Read from the Torah» means reading from the scroll. «The laws of the Torah» means the rules Jews follow. A Torah scroll is a hand-written copy kept in the ark of a synagogue.
explain: Respect shows in how the scroll is handled. It is read with a pointer called a yad, so hands never touch the letters. «Exodus is one of the five books of the Torah, so Jews and Christians share the Ten Commandments.» Christians have the same five books at the start of the Old Testament.
fact: The Torah is the first five books of the Hebrew Bible.
fact: The five books are Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers and Deuteronomy.
fact: Jews believe God gave the Torah to Moses.
fact: A bar or bat mitzvah child reads from the Torah for the first time.
fact: Torah can also mean all Jewish teaching.
exercise: What is a Torah scroll? | *A hand-written copy of the Torah, kept in a synagogue | A printed book of football rules | A type of bread eaten on Sundays
exercise: Who do Jews believe God gave the Torah to? | *Moses | Jesus | Abraham
exercise: Why is the Torah read with a yad? | *So hands do not touch the letters | To make the scroll lighter | To count the pages | To wave at friends
test: «Exodus is one of the five books of the Torah.» How many books are in the Torah? | Seven | Three | Ten | *Five
test: Which festival has people dancing with the Torah? | Easter | *Simchat Torah | Christmas | Diwali
exam: Which of these is one of the five books of the Torah? | Psalms | Matthew | Acts | *Leviticus
